  "worked_solution": "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}[2f(t)+4g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=2{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+4{\\int }_{0}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[2f(t)+4g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =2{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+4{\\int }_{0}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\u27e8-3,\\,\\sqrt{2},\\,2\u27e9+4\u27e8-\\frac{3}{2},\\,-\\frac{1}{4},\\,1\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-6,\\,2\\sqrt{2},\\,4\u27e9+\u27e8-6,\\,-1,\\,4\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-12,\\,2\\sqrt{2}-1,\\,8\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
